Twenty-seven tcl call sites in OpenROAD name a command by a unique prefix
of its real name -- utl::metric_int for utl::metric_integer,
sta::check_positive_int for sta::check_positive_integer, grt::clear for
grt::clear_route_guides, the syn::*_cmd and cgt::*_cmd swig bindings
without their suffix, upf::set_power_switch_port for _map.  None of them
is a command: each resolved through OpenSTA's global unknown handler,
which tries an unknown name as an abbreviation.  With that handler
scoped to read_sdc (patches/0003-opensta-read-sdc-scoped-unknown.patch)
the first of them the flow reaches, report_floating_nets at the place
stage, fails with invalid command name "utl::metric_int".

Spell each one out.  Every site was found by dumping the command set of
the built binary and checking every command token in src/**/*.tcl
against it; a token that is not a command but a unique prefix of one is
an abbreviation.  Behaviour is identical on either interpreter.

Submitted upstream as OpenROAD PR #11439.  Retires on a //:bump onto
an OpenROAD carrying it.

